Third-party components
----------------------

Oboe — Apache License 2.0
  https://github.com/google/oboe
  The audio driver's stream. Apache 2.0 is compatible with GPLv3 (and not
  with GPLv2, which is why this project is GPLv3-or-later).
  Licence text: licences/Apache-2.0.txt

LAME 3.100 — GNU Library General Public License, version 2
  https://lame.sourceforge.io/
  MP3 encoding. Vendored under app/src/main/cpp/third_party/lame and built
  as its own libmp3lame.so, linked against and never compiled in, which is
  the relinking freedom the LGPL asks for; LGPLv2 §3 is what lets a copy be
  taken under GPLv3-or-later. See that directory's PROVENANCE.md.
  Licence text: app/src/main/cpp/third_party/lame/COPYING

Ableton Link 4.0 — GNU General Public License, version 2 or later
  https://github.com/Ableton/link
  A tempo, a beat and a bar line shared with other machines on the same
  network. Dual-licensed: the GPL, or a proprietary licence from Ableton.
  This app takes the GPL, which is what GPLv3-or-later may do with
  GPLv2-or-later code. Vendored under app/src/main/cpp/third_party/link;
  header-only, so it is compiled into libacidulous.so.
  Licence text: licences/GPL-2.0.txt

asio 1.36.0 — Boost Software License 1.0
  https://github.com/chriskohlhoff/asio
  The sockets and timers Link is built on; it comes with Link and is used
  header-only. Vendored under app/src/main/cpp/third_party/asio.
  Licence text: app/src/main/cpp/third_party/asio/LICENSE_1_0.txt

miniaudio 0.11.22 — public domain (the Unlicense), or MIT No Attribution
  https://miniaud.io/
  The desktop build's audio driver, in place of Oboe: PulseAudio, ALSA or
  JACK. Header-only, compiled into the desktop's libacidulous.so and not
  into the phone's. Either licence is the licensee's choice; neither asks for
  a notice. See app/src/main/cpp/third_party/miniaudio/PROVENANCE.md.

alsa-lib 1.2.14 — GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.1 or later
  https://www.alsa-project.org/
  MIDI on Linux, through ALSA's sequencer: the desktop build only. Its headers
  are vendored under app/src/main/cpp/third_party/alsa; the library itself is
  the system's libasound, opened at run time and never compiled in. See that
  directory's PROVENANCE.md.
  Licence text: licences/LGPL-2.1.txt

